                        "form": "more brumous"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "b92766a2-87eb-4e5e-948b-fd13811a5985",
                        "entry_id": "5f026e22-0b40-35bc-8aba-33be62fdf318",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most brumous"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "51f63f43-cbba-37f9-a22a-67f1d7dc7ef8",
                        "entry_id": "5f026e22-0b40-35bc-8aba-33be62fdf318",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Foggy or misty; wintry."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f703a365-7651-4998-9e1e-475e288c787e",
                                "sense_id": "51f63f43-cbba-37f9-a22a-67f1d7dc7ef8",
                                "text": "The blond misses of Albion see nothing in the dull inhabitants of their brumous isle, which can compare with the ardour and vivacity of the children of the South. We bring our sunshine with us; we are Frenchmen, and accustomed to conquer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "256c9d2b-99b7-4dd1-a0dc-a530c512597f",
                                "sense_id": "51f63f43-cbba-37f9-a22a-67f1d7dc7ef8",
                                "text": "One of the greatest charms of fox-hunting undoubtedly is, that it disposes of all the dirty weather which goes to make up three-fourths of an English winter. Wet, and drizzle, and muggy fog (the characteristics of our brumous and insular climate, according to numerous French authorities), are the capital on which it trades. To the hunting man a rainy morning in winter […] means sport, and society, and enjoyment."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f537f2e-5551-424c-bbd5-6208b565ac7e",
                                "sense_id": "51f63f43-cbba-37f9-a22a-67f1d7dc7ef8",
                                "text": "The Golden Gate was hardly to be seen at all, except on very favorable days, for the thick veil of ocean mist which hung over it. The whole scene was dull, sombre, brumous, depressing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b555cc8-e168-434a-8710-c6c7461af112",
                                "sense_id": "51f63f43-cbba-37f9-a22a-67f1d7dc7ef8",
                                "text": "Let us compare these observations made in our brumous latitudes with those effected by Father [Angelo] Secchi with the fine equatorial of the Roman Observatory."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "185e4528-7680-46b8-90ee-d56247c90aa0",
                                "sense_id": "51f63f43-cbba-37f9-a22a-67f1d7dc7ef8",
                                "text": "She worked under the great tapestry with its glowing but subdued tones—huntsmen with lofted horns had been running down a female stag. After the rape, leaving the grooms to bring the trophy home, they galloped away into the soft brumous Italian skyline; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0038c00a-4cde-43b9-b88a-371a2b2b1ee2",
                        "source_entry_id": "5f026e22-0b40-35bc-8aba-33be62fdf318",
                        "source_sense_id": "51f63f43-cbba-37f9-a22a-67f1d7dc7ef8",
                        "source_sense_description": "foggy or misty — see also foggy, misty",
                        "target_lang_word": "brumeux",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "brumeux",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8938c881-cb85-3679-9d80-26a6179c5ef4",
                                        "entry_id": "bcbf3fef-832a-3aab-933c-b28aa02f7c94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est chargé de brume."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78683404-3433-48af-8273-957b22430533",
                                                "sense_id": "8938c881-cb85-3679-9d80-26a6179c5ef4",
                                                "text": "Le temps, changé, était devenu calme, brumeux, morne."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c91eba3-3adb-430e-8c85-b1c2e76e7ef3",
                                                "sense_id": "8938c881-cb85-3679-9d80-26a6179c5ef4",
                                                "text": "Le ciel, clair au départ de Saint-Louis, devient brumeux vers Dakar. Nous apercevons dans un trou le feu de la pointe du Cap-Vert, à 4 heures."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0223c790-72a8-3e49-a49c-f2c469309ee5",
                                        "entry_id": "bcbf3fef-832a-3aab-933c-b28aa02f7c94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui est comme chargé de brume."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "acfbb6a3-8346-45d2-9b35-4689ec69c1be",
                                                "sense_id": "0223c790-72a8-3e49-a49c-f2c469309ee5",
                                                "text": "Sauf que ce qu’elle omet, c’est que ce n’est pas auprès d’elle que je vais devoir faire mes preuves, mais auprès d’une psy attachiante, aux yeux brumeux, orageux et sauvages et pourtant si clairs, mélangés aux miens, si bleus et finalement si sombres."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d20cce5d-583b-365d-af20-7f4de42f8543",
                                        "entry_id": "bcbf3fef-832a-3aab-933c-b28aa02f7c94",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Peu clair, voire obscur (en parlant par exemple d’un discours)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9efd4ee9-f362-432a-ab0d-59e1c95fbf6b",
                                                "sense_id": "d20cce5d-583b-365d-af20-7f4de42f8543",
                                                "text": "À un moment donné, pour des raisons que je ne saurais expliquer, je me laissai épouser. Ça ne dura pas plus de six mois, et cette expérience me paraît aujourd’hui si brumeuse que j’ai de la peine à me rappeler de quoi ma femme avait l’air."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
